Recommends: arp-scan, iputils-ping
Suggests: git
Description: continuous auditor for your own local network
 lanwatch discovers the devices on your LAN, inventories their open services,
 evaluates rules against what it finds and reports changes and findings through
 a local web UI and notifications. An optional local LLM (Ollama) explains
 findings; nothing leaves the network unless you enable it.
 .
 The package is self-contained: it ships its own Python interpreter and
 libraries under /usr/lib/lanwatch. The service runs as an unprivileged user
 without capabilities; scans that need raw sockets go through a small
 socket-activated helper that holds CAP_NET_RAW and nothing else.
